_vl53l7cx_poll_for_mcu_boot() must not report success for a boot it did not see.

This is 0002's defect in the other place it lives, found by auditing what
vl53l7cx_init() actually treats as success. The MCU boot wait polls GO2 status 0
for bit 7 with a 1 ms wait, up to 500 times, and if the loop runs out it falls
through to `return status` WITHOUT SETTING ANYTHING. Every read having succeeded,
status is VL53L7CX_STATUS_OK -- so a device whose MCU never boots reports a
successful boot wait.

It also did `status |= go2_status1`, the same OR of a DEVICE REGISTER into a
status byte that 0002 had to remove from vl53l7cx_stop_ranging(): the ULD's own
codes live in those 8 bits, so a device byte of 0x01 is indistinguishable from
TIMEOUT_ERROR and 0xFF from STATUS_ERROR.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM. init() checks `if(status != 0) goto exit` right after
the call, and the next step polls UI_CMD_STATUS through
_vl53l7cx_poll_for_answer(), which DOES report its timeout. So a non-booting MCU
was probably still caught, one step later and 2 s further on, as a UI command
that did not answer. The defect is therefore misattribution rather than silent
success -- which is exactly the failure this driver's bench work has spent its
rounds removing, and the reason a boot that did not happen must say so itself.

ONLY LOOP EXHAUSTION BECOMES A TIMEOUT. The loop has three exits and they are not
the same event: bit 7 set is a boot that answered, bit 0 set is upstream's
separate "stop waiting" condition whose meaning is not changed here, and running
out of iterations is the one that had no report. A `timeout >= 500` test after
the loop would have mislabelled a bit-0 exit that happened on the last
iteration, so the two early exits mark themselves instead.

And an error already recorded is kept: a transport failure during polling stays
the status rather than being overwritten by the timeout, which is the ordering
0002 settled.

--- a/modules/vl53l7cx_api.c
+++ b/modules/vl53l7cx_api.c
@@ -63,24 +63,34 @@
               VL53L7CX_Configuration      *p_dev)
 {
    uint8_t go2_status0, go2_status1, status = VL53L7CX_STATUS_OK;
+   uint8_t left_early = 0;
    uint16_t timeout = 0;
 
    do {
 		status |= VL53L7CX_RdByte(&(p_dev->platform), 0x06, &go2_status0);
 		if((go2_status0 & (uint8_t)0x80) != (uint8_t)0){
 			status |= VL53L7CX_RdByte(&(p_dev->platform), 0x07, &go2_status1);
-			status |= go2_status1;
+			if((go2_status1 != (uint8_t)0)
+				&& (status == VL53L7CX_STATUS_OK)){
+				status = VL53L7CX_STATUS_ERROR;
+			}
+			left_early = 1;
 			break;
 		}
 		(void)VL53L7CX_WaitMs(&(p_dev->platform), 1);
 		timeout++;
 
 		if((go2_status0 & (uint8_t)0x1) != (uint8_t)0){
+			left_early = 1;
 			break;
 		}
 
 	}while (timeout < (uint16_t)500);
 
+   if((left_early == (uint8_t)0) && (status == VL53L7CX_STATUS_OK)){
+      status = VL53L7CX_STATUS_TIMEOUT_ERROR;
+   }
+
    return status;
 }
 
